 not been reviewed by the authors.","citation_ids":["cite.euler.lemma-a.2"],"evidence_ids":["link.euler.lemma-a.2"],"id":"euler.lemma-a.2","kind":"claim","label":"Lemma A.2","locator":"Lemma A.2, Section A","source_id":"paper","statement":"**Lemma A.2.** Let either $H=\\mathbb R^3$, $\\mathcal R=\\mathbb P$, or $H=L^2(I;\\mathbb R^3)$, $\\mathcal R=\\mathbb P\\mathcal Q$, where $\\mathcal Qv=v-\\int_0^1v(t)\\,\\mathrm dt$. Let $B\\in C^{1,1/2}(\\mathbb T^3;\\mathcal L(H))$ and $\\mu>0$. Suppose $$\\begin{equation}\n \\langle B(a)w,w\\rangle_H\\ge\\mu\\left\\lVert w\\right\\rVert_H^2 \\tag{A.4}\n\\end{equation}$$ for every $a\\in\\mathbb T^3$ and every $w\\in H$, with $\\mathcal Qw=w$ in the second case. Then $\\mathcal RB$ is an isomorphism on $\\mathcal RC^{0,1/2}(\\mathbb T^3;H)$, and $$\\begin{equation}\n \\left\\lVert v\\right\\rVert_{C^{0,1/2}_a(H)}\n \\le C(2+\\mu^{-1}+\\left\\lVert B\\right\\rVert_{C^1_a\\mathcal L(H)})^{p}\n            \\left\\lVert\\mathcal RBv\\right\\rVert_{C^{0,1/2}_a(H)}. \\tag{A.5}\n\\end{equation}$$ If moreover $B\\in C^{k,1/2}(\\mathbb T^3;\\mathcal L(H))$ for an integer $k\\ge1$, the same operator is an isomorphism on $\\mathcal RC^{k,1/2}(\\mathbb T^3;H)$.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:db48fdd5ba2604749972848ed79e43c2768fdab18b46be5a44ed5375dec0afe1/nodes/euler.lemma-a.2","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:db48fdd5ba2604749972848ed79e43c2768fdab18b46be5a44ed5375dec0afe1/nodes/euler.lemma-a.2","id":"sha256:db48fdd5ba2604749972848ed79e43c2768fdab18b46be5a44ed5375dec0afe1/edges/%5B%22euler.lemma-a.2%22%2C%22lean.TorusEuler.Paper.Statement.lemma_A_2%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:db48fdd5ba2604749972848ed79e43c2768fdab18b46be5a44ed5375dec0afe1/edges/%5B%22euler.lemma-a.2%22%2C%22lean.TorusEuler.Paper.Statement.lemma_A_2%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:db48fdd5ba2604749972848ed79e43c2768fdab18b46be5a44ed5375d